  "notes": [
    "The baseline is full-corpus Hilbert bulk construction at production leaf capacity. The production lake incremental ingestion path is a separate baseline.",
    "Spooled arms stream the corpus from the normalized file through checksummed partitions. The Hilbert full-build baseline holds its prepared float32 plane in memory.",
    "Both sampled algorithms use the same root reservoir selection, fixed seed, router fanout limits and terminal construction machinery.",
    "Training row counts accumulate across hierarchy nodes and can include repeated corpus members.",
    "The spooled HBC allocator is shared by construction and native publication and enforces a 256 MiB live-allocation limit. Process RSS includes mmap residency, file pages and allocator overhead.",
    "Each successful build publishes native authority, reopens it, and verifies tree links and active member count.",
    "The stored query sweeps were repeated against the completed generations using the same disk-backed vector loader and bounded retained caches for all three algorithms.",
    "The 95.5 percent target uses the first measured probe count at or above the target, with unequal recall at those selected points.",
    "Trials ran serially on a shared workstation. Query timings and build timings are observations without controlled statistical speedup claims.",
    "Local build times start from prepared normalized inputs. Remote I/O, Parquet normalization, exact-vector LSM construction and lake artifact upload are measured separately.",
    "Construction trials precede the final origin/main merge. The artifact records the tested executable hash."
  ],
